  "title": "tshark: Reassure Coverity",
  "description": "process_cap_file is a static function, we only call it in one place,\nand only after cf_open succeeds. That guarantees that cf->provider.wth\nis not NULL (cf_open always returns failure if cf->provider.wth is\nNULL.) Coverity apparently has trouble tracing that logic. If wth\nwere somehow NULL there, then there would be some null pointer\ndereferences, but it isn't and so there aren't. Reassure Coverity\nwith an assertion.\n\nCoverity CID 1450449\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
